# Benchy — Coding Standards

## Style

- Match existing JSX/JS patterns; do not migrate files to TypeScript unless asked.
- Prefer maintainable, local changes over drive-by refactors.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies — the stack is intentionally small.
- Explain non-obvious scientific or persistence logic with brief comments when needed.

## Protected formulas and data (do not “improve”)

Do **not** change these without explicit user approval **and** relevant tests:

| Area | Location |
|------|----------|
| Gel Fiji/Excel background, corrected, ratio | `src/apps/gel-quantification/engine/fijiExcelWorkflow.js` |
| Gel IntDen / grayscale | `measurements.js`, `fijiConstants.js` |
| qPCR ΔΔCt / RQ | `src/apps/qpcr-insight/utils/computeDDCt.js` |
| Endpoint categories A–I | `src/apps/endpoint-analysis/constants/categories.js` |
| CFU | `src/apps/colony-counter/utils/cfu.js` |
| Dilution / master-mix | `src/shared/labCalculators.js` |
| Strain reference | `src/shared/data/strains.json` |
| `.benchy` schema | `src/shared/persistence/labtoolsSchema.js` |

After gel math changes: `npm run test:gel`. After persistence/schema: `npm run test:persistence`.

## Tooling

- Node `>=22.9`, npm 11 lockfile — run `npm run validate:lock` / do not hand-edit lockfile casually.
- Do not skip husky hooks unless the user explicitly asks.
